ASoC: tas2783: expose DSP posture and UDMPU cluster as kcontrols

Base: Linux v7.2-rc5, sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c
      (verified 2026-08-04: this is the only difference between that file
      and src/tas2783/tas2783-sdw.c in this repo; tas2783.h is unmodified)

On the ASUS ProArt PX13 (HN7306EAC) the ACPI firmware omits the SDCA
function-type DisCo constant, so find_sdca_function() fails and the
per-amp init tables, which set DSP posture 1 on one amp and 4 on the
other for left/right channel selection, are never applied. Both amps
then render the same channel.

These controls let userspace apply the postures; this repo's UCM file
sets 1 and 4 in the Speaker EnableSequence. The proper fix is a
function-type fallback in sound/soc/sdca/sdca_functions.c (see
docs/kernel-fix-plan.md).

Regenerate after changing src/tas2783/ by diffing against the matching
stock kernel file with a/ b/ prefixes.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c
@@ -560,6 +560,19 @@
 	SOC_SINGLE_RANGE_EXT_TLV("Speaker Volume", TAS2783_DVC_LVL,
 				 0, 0, 200, 1, tas2783_digital_getvol,
 				 tas2783_digital_putvol, tas2781_dvc_tlv),
+	/*
+	 * The DSP posture selects which channel of the stereo stream this
+	 * amp renders; the ACPI init tables intend posture 1 for the first
+	 * amp and 4 for the second, but are not applied because the SDCA
+	 * function parse fails on this firmware.
+	 */
+	SOC_SINGLE("DSP Posture Select",
+		   SDW_SDCA_CTL(1, TAS2783_SDCA_ENT_PPU21, 0x10, 0),
+		   0, 15, 0),
+	SOC_SINGLE("UDMPU Cluster Select",
+		   SDW_SDCA_CTL(1, TAS2783_SDCA_ENT_UDMPU23,
+				TAS2783_SDCA_CTL_UDMPU_CLUSTER, 0),
+		   0, 3, 0),
 };
 
 static s32 tas2783_validate_calibdata(struct tas2783_prv *tas_dev,
